From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Zach Taylor <zctaylor.work@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 17:29:40 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 19/30] Deny egress paths that a server might decode to another
 path

A request path is matched raw, so a server that decodes it can read a
different path than the one a rule matched. unsafePath now uses one closed
grammar. A path is denied when it holds ";" or a backslash, a malformed
escape, an escape of an unreserved byte or of "%", "/", "\" or ";", an
escape that decodes to invalid UTF-8, a "." or ".." segment, or a decoded
form that NFKC changes or that holds a control character. This closes
"..;x", "%252e", "%EF%BC%8E" and "%00" on the credential-selection path.

CheckExactPath applies the same grammar to exact paths. The proto and
guide list the denied forms.

Fork-Topic: egress-paths
Fork-Upstream: candidate
